Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:34:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Advertise interface transfer-impedance layers as a worker
 capability

The Julia side validates requests against the schema only, and boundary
parameters are open, so an engine without the layer accepts
boundary.parameters["transfer_impedance"] and solves as if it were not
there. Clients must be able to tell before they submit.

- worker-v1.json advertises "optional_physics": ["interface_transfer_impedance"].
- negotiate_submission refuses a request that carries a layer unless the
  worker advertises it; validate_worker_ready checks the new list.
- Conformance case coupled_interface_transfer_impedance_layer: the layer
  on the bounded interface boundary is a valid compiled system.
- Version 0.3.0+ti1 in pyproject, __version__ and worker-v1.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
